
<h1>LGD USA Supplier Fetch</h1>

<div class="panel">
  <p>Import LGD USA jewelry products into Our Jewel Catalog V2. No Shopify products are created or modified.</p>

  <p><strong>Minimum interval:</strong> 15 minutes between attempts, including unsuccessful requests.</p>

  <p><strong>Last attempt:</strong>
    <%= @state.last_attempt_at ? l(@state.last_attempt_at) : "Never" %>
  </p>

  <p><strong>Next allowed:</strong>
    <%= @state.eligible_at ? l(@state.eligible_at) : "Now" %>
  </p>

  <p><strong>Catalog products:</strong> <%= SupplierProduct.count %></p>

  <% if @state.can_fetch? && (Rails.env.production? || (Rails.env.development? && request.local?)) %>
    <%= button_to "Fetch LGD USA Products",
          supplier_fetches_path,
          method: :post,
          data: {
            turbo_confirm: "Make one supplier API request now? The next request will be blocked for 15 minutes."
          } %>
  <% else %>
    <p>Fetch is unavailable until the 15-minute cooldown expires or the application is running in an authorized environment.</p>
  <% end %>

  <p class="muted">
    Only page 1 is requested. Do not click repeatedly.
    Confirm the number of products before implementing pagination.
  </p>
</div>
